# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[help]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
help_text = Systematics TRILLION MIDI maker
================================

1. Click the document in the middle to choose a MIDI file.
2. In File properties, tick the track(s) you want to multiply.
3. Set the track multiplier (1 to 65,535).
4. Press Start.

What it does
------------
Each ticked (selected) track is repeated your chosen number of times;
unticked tracks are kept exactly once. So a melody track can stay the
same while a "spam" track is multiplied up to 65,535 times. The total
track count is capped at 65,535 (the MIDI limit), so when other tracks
are kept the multiplier is reduced automatically to fit.

Multiple tracks
---------------
Multi-track MIDI files are supported. Open File properties to see every
track (with its note count and name) and choose which ones get
multiplied. Your selection is remembered per file.

Why compress?
--------------
The uncompressed result can be many gigabytes, but because every track
is identical it compresses to almost nothing. Settings let you pick the
archive format: .xz (default), .gz, .bz2, .zst, .zip or .7z. Decompress
it with any tool that understands the format (7-Zip opens them all) to
get the full multi-track .mid back.

Fast mode
---------
Streamed mode (default) compresses the whole file in one pass and gives
the smallest output. Fast mode compresses the track once and repeats
that block (concatenated XZ/gzip/bzip2/zstd streams, or repeated zip
entries) — it is nearly instant but larger. 7z is always a single
compression pass (the format has no repeat-block trick), so huge
multipliers are slower in 7z — prefer xz/gz/zip for giant black midis.

Compression presets run from 0 (fastest, larger) to 9 (slowest, smallest).

Compression passes
------------------
In Settings, choose how many times the file is recompressed: 1 (plain,
e.g. .gz), 2 (double, .gz.xz) or 3 (triple, .gz.xz.xz). Each extra pass
recompresses the previous file with XZ and shrinks Fast-mode output
dramatically. Decompress the same number of times to get the .mid back.

Memory
------
Choosing a file loads every track into RAM, so a 100 MB file uses
roughly 100 MB of memory (1 GB file = ~1 GB of RAM). This is why
repeated runs are instant: the tracks are never re-read from disk.

Theme
-----
Switch between dark and light mode in Settings. The change applies as
soon as you save.

Updates
-------
The app checks its built-in update feed (hosted on GitHub Pages) on
startup, and you can press Settings > Check for updates any time. When
a newer version is found you can download and install it in one click
— the app backs up the old files and restarts itself.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[about]
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
about_text = {app_name}
Version {version}

Turns a MIDI into a gigantic multi-track black MIDI by multiplying
the tracks you choose, compressed into a tiny .xz file.

Built with Python + tkinter. Have fun!
